# Build-context exclusions for `service/Dockerfile`, whose context is this
# directory rather than the repository root.
#
# The context is small today and none of these match anything committed. They
# are here for what a working tree accumulates: a build context is copied to
# the daemon whole, and anything in it can be read by any stage and can end up
# in a layer. A credential that reaches a layer is published with the image and
# is not removed by deleting it in a later stage.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Local build output, if anyone builds into the module rather than out of it.
bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Nothing the compiler reads.
*.md
